    "html": "<p>A thin layer of transparent oil with a refractive index of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.40\"></span> is spread over a pool of water, which has a refractive index of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.33\"></span>. The oil layer is illuminated at normal incidence by monochromatic light with a wavelength of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"560\\ \\text{nm}\"></span> in air. Which of the following is the minimum non-zero thickness of the oil layer required for the reflected light to experience constructive interference?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"140\\ \\text{nm}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100\\ \\text{nm}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"280\\ \\text{nm}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\\ \\text{nm}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
